The '''Kraken''' is a [[Grineer]] burst pistol that fires two shots with one trigger pull, and is highly accurate at range.

This weapon can be sold for {{cc|5,000}}; it is also a [[weapon crafting ingredient]] for {{Weapon|Kulstar}}.
{{Checklist|nocategory=true|
* {{Weapon|Kraken}} → {{Weapon|Kulstar}}
}}

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Impact}} damage.

{{Advantages|
*High accuracy.
*High ammo efficiency.
}}

{{Disadvantages|
*Linearly less efficient &ndash; sometimes a target may only die with three bullets, which requires an entire second burst to be fired.
}}

{{WeaponComparison|Kuva Kraken}}

==Acquisition==
The Kraken's blueprint can be purchased from the [[Market]]. Alternatively, it can be acquired from completing the [[Mars]] to [[Phobos]] [[Junction]].

{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

==Notes==
*The weapon's high {{D|Impact|icon=Impact}} damage makes it effective against the [[Grineer]].

==Tips==
*Kraken shoots two bullets in quick succession. Practice is recommended to fully master this weapon. Increasing the weapons rate of fire also decreases the gap between the bullets' firings.
*One can drop their aim to negate the kick on the second shot. With practice it is possible to snipe ranged targets, hitting with all bullets. If the first shot is aimed for the chest region, the recoil will knock the second bullet up, resulting in a headshot. 
*{{M|Steady Hands}} can be used to negate the weapon's recoil, tightening the weapon's shot grouping per burst resulting in better accuracy at range. This can be beneficial for landing both shots in each burst.
*Like the {{Weapon|Sicarus}} pistol which also fires in bursts, timing is key to acquire maximum fire rate. Do not spam the fire button as the fire rate will be nearly half of what it should be. Instead, time your clicks accordingly to get the hang of when to correctly press the fire button. 
*There is a small delay after firing where reloading can occur, unlike most weapons, so usually tapping the reload button after firing will not work and you must either double tap or wait a moment before reloading. This can be very annoying, and it is the same for the Sicarus as well. 
*Kraken's average [[critical chance]] is alleviated by having a high critical multiplier. Although the weapon is not ideal for a critically focused build, it rewards players who get consistent headshots.

==Trivia==
*The [[wikipedia:Kraken|Kraken]] is a massive sea monster in [[wikipedia:Norse mythology|Norse mythology]], which is said to dwell off the coasts of Norway and Greenland.
*The large bulb in the front of the weapon with a cable running to it might be a flashlight of some sort, or possibly an infrared bulb. It could also be part of a targeting system, possibly connected to the [[Seeker]]s visor.

