===Elemental Bonus===

The Kuva weapons additionally have bonus damage of one damage type which can either be {{D|Impact}}, {{D|Heat}}, {{D|Cold}}, {{D|Electricity}}, {{D|Toxin}}, {{D|Magnetic}}, or {{D|Radiation}}, ranging from 25-60% of the weapon's '''base damage''' determined randomly.<ref name="bonus_chance">"The bonus Valence Bonus percentage roll on Kuva Lich and Sisters of Parvos Adversary Weapons is now properly randomized! Previously, the roll was weighted towards lower values, meaning a lot of progenitor runs for slim chance at a high percentage Valence Bonus. Now, it is entirely randomized to give players equal chance across the bonus range." - {{ver|42}} patch notes</ref> The damage type of this bonus damage is determined by the Progenitor Warframe, as per [[Adversary System/Progenitor|this table]]. This additional bonus damage applies as weapon base damage, meaning elemental mods and status that scale from base / modified base damage will be affected.

A rank 40 Kuva weapon can be applied with a {{Resource|Elemental Vice}} that enables the Valence Override option, which allows swapping between the bonus damage types freely. This does not affect the damage percentage.

